## Coverage and source rule

- **Excalidraw:** 7 unique sources, all 7 visible, with canonical local `.excalidraw` files.
- **Mermaid:** 27 unique sources, all 27 visible, with canonical local `.mmd` files.

The Excalidraw source remains authoritative for visual layout; the generated SVG is a review surface. Mermaid source remains authoritative for Mermaid views. Duplicate package copies are provenance evidence, not separate diagrams.

## Text alternative

An owner request moves through intake, business definition, product, UX, architecture, security, and repository research. An approved work unit enters the broker. The broker chooses a provider, reserves the other provider for critique, isolates implementation, runs real checks, gathers fresh reviews, returns defects to the owning role, and stops at human release authority. The secure delivery path separates untrusted authoring, deterministic pull-request checks, protected main, immutable artifact promotion, environment approval, production verification, rollback, and evidence.

## Edit and regenerate

The canonical sources are served from this Decision System. Download a local `.excalidraw` source and open it in [Excalidraw](https://excalidraw.com/) for editing or [Excalidraw Animate](https://dai-shi.github.io/excalidraw-animate/) for animation review. Regenerate committed previews with `npm run docs:diagrams:public`.
